 "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T00:11:14.218Z",
 "source_selection": "Orden PEJ/331/2025 (BOA no. 65, 3 April 2025) declares the 'Tillion Aragón' data-centre campus in Villamayor de Gállego, promoted by Máquina Solar SL (wholly owned by Grupo Azora), an investment of autonomous and general interest: 79.6 ha of rural land in 23 parcels of cadastral polygon 46, bounded by the A-129 to the south-east and the Camino de Carbonera to the north-west. Orden PEJ/415/2026 (BOA no. 47, 10 March 2026) republishes the updated delimitation as annex I: 23 polygon 46 references plus parcel 31/72 for the fiscal metering station. All were retrieved individually from the Catastro INSPIRE WFS (GetParcel). The annex prints reference 50306A046000050000RE against parcel number 37; the locator uses parcel 46/37 (50306A04600037), which adjoins the other 22, rather than 46/5 (50306A04600005), which lies 3.4 m from them; both captures are kept and the choice moves the centroid by about 10 m. Parcel 31/72 (metering station near SET Peñaflor) is excluded from the centroid. The union of the whole cadastral parcels (123.30 ha) is larger than the declared 79.6 ha because the delimitation covers parts of some parcels.",
